<div class="container-fluid px-4 py-6">
    <div class="mb-6">
        {{> msgStatus}}
    </div>

    <div class="ui-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <h1 class="text-2xl font-bold text-gray-800 mb-2">API docs — key management</h1>
        <p class="doc-section" style="margin-bottom:0">Use a <strong>personal API key</strong> to create, list, read, update,
        reset and delete <strong>licence keys</strong> from your own website or Telegram bot.
        Creating a key through the API charges your saldo exactly like the panel does.</p>
        <p class="doc-note" style="margin-top:14px">This API is <strong>only for keys</strong>. It cannot change the mod name,
        status text, floating text, features, maintenance mode or any other server setting.
        For the loader / mod side, see <a href="/docs">Integration docs</a>.</p>
        <p style="margin-top:14px"><a href="/api-keys" class="ui-btn">Create / manage my API keys</a></p>
    </div>

    <div class="ui-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>1. Get an API key</h2>
            <p>Log in to the panel, open <a href="/api-keys">API keys</a>, give the key a name (for example
            <span class="doc-inline">my-telegram-bot</span>) and press <strong>Create API key</strong>.
            The token starts with <span class="doc-inline">amk_</span> and is shown <strong>once</strong> — copy it immediately.
            Only its SHA-256 hash is stored, so it cannot be recovered later. You can revoke or delete it at any time.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>2. Base URL + authentication</h2>
            <code class="doc-url">{{apiBase}}/api/v1</code>
            <p>Send the token on <strong>every</strong> request as the <span class="doc-inline">X-API-Key</span> header
            (<span class="doc-inline">Authorization: Bearer &lt;token&gt;</span> also works). No cookies, no session, no CSRF token.
            CORS is open, so a browser site on another domain can call it directly.</p>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>X-API-Key: amk_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE
Content-Type: application/json</code></pre>
            <p>Missing or revoked key → <span class="doc-inline">401</span>. A key whose owner is banned or expired → <span class="doc-inline">403</span>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>3. Response shape</h2>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>// success
{ "ok": true, "keys": [ ... ], "total": 2, "limit": 50, "offset": 0 }

// failure
{ "ok": false, "error": { "code": "insufficient_balance", "message": "Insufficient balance" } }</code></pre>
            <p>Always check <span class="doc-inline">ok</span> and the HTTP status. Errors are JSON, never HTML.</p>
        </div>
    </div>

    <div class="ui-card rounded-2xl p-6 sm:p-8 mb-6">
        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>4. Endpoints</h2>
            <div class="table-scroll">
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>Method</th><th>Path</th><th>What it does</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1</span></td><td>Endpoint index + your API key name</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/me</span></td><td>Account saldo / level and API key info</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/pricing</span></td><td>Available durations and price per device</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/keys</span></td><td>List your keys (pagination + filters)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>POST</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/keys</span></td><td><strong>Create keys</strong> — charges saldo</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>GET</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/keys/{user_key}</span></td><td>One key with its device list</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>POST / PATCH</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/keys/{user_key}</span></td><td>Update devices / duration / game / status / device list (free)</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>POST</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/keys/{user_key}/reset</span></td><td>Clear all bound devices</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>DELETE</td><td><span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/keys/{user_key}</span></td><td>Delete a key</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
            <p style="margin-top:12px">You can only see and manage keys <strong>your account created</strong>.
            List filters: <span class="doc-inline">?limit=50&amp;offset=0&amp;game=PUBG&amp;status=1</span>.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>5. Create a key (curl)</h2>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>curl -sS -X POST {{apiBase}}/api/v1/keys \
  -H 'X-API-Key: amk_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE' \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"game":"PUBG","duration":24,"max_devices":1}'
</code></pre>
            <p>Body fields: <span class="doc-inline">game</span> (default <span class="doc-inline">PUBG</span>),
            <span class="doc-inline">duration</span> (hours: 2, 5, 24, 72, 168, 336, 720),
            <span class="doc-inline">max_devices</span> (1–100), optional <span class="doc-inline">count</span> (1–100)
            and optional <span class="doc-inline">custom_key</span> (4–19 chars, letters/digits/<span class="doc-inline">_</span>/<span class="doc-inline">-</span>).</p>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>{
  "ok": true,
  "keys": [
    {
      "id": 3, "user_key": "admin-24-aB3dE", "game": "PUBG",
      "duration": 24, "max_devices": 1, "status": 1,
      "devices": [], "device_count": 0, "expired_date": null,
      "created_at": "2026-11-05T10:30:00.000Z", "updated_at": "2026-11-05T10:30:00.000Z"
    }
  ],
  "count": 1, "price": 80, "currency": "INR",
  "saldo_before": 2147384644, "saldo_after": 2147384564, "charged": 80
}</code></pre>
            <p class="doc-note"><strong>Saldo rule:</strong> <span class="doc-inline">price = price_per_device(duration) × max_devices × count</span>. Every key is charged.
            The debit and all key inserts run in one database transaction: if anything fails, no keys are created and nothing is charged.
            Repeating the same <span class="doc-inline">request_id</span> returns the original result instead of charging twice.
            Insufficient balance → <span class="doc-inline">402 insufficient_balance</span> and nothing is created.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>6. List / read / update / reset / delete</h2>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code># list
curl -sS {{apiBase}}/api/v1/keys -H 'X-API-Key: amk_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE'

# read one
curl -sS {{apiBase}}/api/v1/keys/admin-24-aB3dE -H 'X-API-Key: amk_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE'

# update (POST or PATCH)
curl -sS -X PATCH {{apiBase}}/api/v1/keys/admin-24-aB3dE \
  -H 'X-API-Key: amk_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE' -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"max_devices":3,"status":1}'

# clear bound devices
curl -sS -X POST {{apiBase}}/api/v1/keys/admin-24-aB3dE/reset \
  -H 'X-API-Key: amk_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE'

# delete
curl -sS -X DELETE {{apiBase}}/api/v1/keys/admin-24-aB3dE \
  -H 'X-API-Key: amk_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE'</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>7. JavaScript fetch example</h2>
            <pre class="doc-code"><code>const BASE = "{{apiBase}}/api/v1";
const TOKEN = "amk_YOUR_TOKEN_HERE";

async function api(path, options = {}) {
  const r = await fetch(BASE + path, {
    ...options,
    headers: { "X-API-Key": TOKEN, "Content-Type": "application/json", ...options.headers }
  });
  const data = await r.json();
  if (!data.ok) throw new Error(data.error.code + ": " + data.error.message);
  return data;
}

const made = await api("/keys", {
  method: "POST",
  body: JSON.stringify({ game: "PUBG", duration: 24, max_devices: 1 })
});
console.log(made.keys[0].user_key, "charged", made.price);</code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>8. Error codes</h2>
            <div class="table-scroll">
                <table>
                    <thead><tr><th>HTTP</th><th>code</th><th>Meaning</th></tr></thead>
                    <tbody>
                        <tr><td>401</td><td><span class="doc-inline">missing_api_key</span>, <span class="doc-inline">invalid_api_key</span></td><td>No key, or revoked/unknown key</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>403</td><td><span class="doc-inline">account_inactive</span>, <span class="doc-inline">account_expired</span></td><td>Key owner account is blocked or expired</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>400</td><td><span class="doc-inline">invalid_request</span></td><td>Bad parameters or no updatable field</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>402</td><td><span class="doc-inline">insufficient_balance</span></td><td>Not enough saldo for the requested keys</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>404</td><td><span class="doc-inline">key_not_found</span>, <span class="doc-inline">not_found</span></td><td>Key does not exist or is not yours</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>405</td><td><span class="doc-inline">method_not_allowed</span></td><td>Wrong HTTP verb for the path</td></tr>
                        <tr><td>409</td><td><span class="doc-inline">key_exists</span>, <span class="doc-inline">balance_conflict</span></td><td>Custom key taken, or concurrent balance change (retry)</td></tr>
                    </tbody>
                </table>
            </div>
        </div>

        <div class="doc-section">
            <h2>9. Good practice</h2>
            <p>Keep the token server-side (bot backend, serverless function), never in public frontend source.
            Use HTTPS, one key per project so you can revoke it independently, and check
            <span class="doc-inline">/api/v1/me</span> before a create to show the current balance.
            Full reference: <span class="doc-inline">API.md</span> in the repo.</p>
        </div>
    </div>
</div>
